    {
      "id": "s3",
      "part": 3,
      "label": "Part 3",
      "instruction": "Talk together with your partner about the situation.",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q3",
          "number": 3,
          "points": 20,
          "skills": [],
          "material": [
            {
              "id": "i2",
              "type": "imageRef",
              "image": "img2"
            }
          ],
          "interaction": {
            "kind": "speaking",
            "prompt": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "Talk with your partner about the different ways two students could get information for a school project about fashion, and decide which would be best."
              }
            ],
            "turns": [
              {
                "id": "t1",
                "text": "Now, in this part of the test you’re going to talk about something together for about two minutes. I’m going to describe a situation to you. Two students are going to do a school project about fashion and they need to get some information for their project. Here are some ways they could get information. Talk together about the different ways they could get information about fashion and say which would be best. All right? Now, talk together.",
                "role": "examiner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t1.mp3",
                  "seconds": 31.9
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t2",
                "text": "Shall I start? I think looking on the internet is a good idea, because there’s lots of information about fashion online. What do you think?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t2.mp3",
                  "seconds": 8.6
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t3",
                "text": "That’s true. What about reading fashion magazines? They have lots of photos of new clothes. Do you agree?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t3.mp3",
                  "seconds": 7.1
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t4",
                "text": "I’m not sure about going to a fashion show. The tickets can be really expensive. What’s your opinion?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t4.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.4
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t5",
                "text": "What about visiting a museum? They could learn about the clothes people wore in the past. Is that a good idea?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t5.mp3",
                  "seconds": 6.6
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t6",
                "text": "They could also try making some clothes themselves, or look in shop windows. Which do you prefer?",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t6.mp3",
                  "seconds": 5.8
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "t7",
                "text": "So, which way do you think would be best? I think the internet, because it’s quick and free.",
                "role": "partner",
                "audio": {
                  "src": "assets/pet1/pet1-t3-s-q3-t7.mp3",
                  "seconds": 5.9
                }
              }
            ],
            "maxSeconds": 45,
            "scoring": "judge"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
